# NoiseBot camera experiment profile: OV2640 DVP raw VGA.
#
# Purpose:
# - Tests whether the DVP/raw path can capture VGA at all on this board.
# - This is NOT the stable product baseline and should not replace
#   sdkconfig.defaults unless the hardware validation below passes.
#
# Expected tradeoff:
# - Native frame: YUV422 640x480 at nominal 6 FPS.
# - Frame payload is much larger than 240x240 YUV422, and software JPEG encode
#   will be expensive. This is a diagnostic experiment for snapshot/analyze,
#   not a monitoring default.
#
# How to use from a clean config:
#   Rename or remove sdkconfig, then configure with both defaults files:
#   idf.py -DSDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.experiment.ov2640-yuv422-640x480.defaults" reconfigure
#   idf.py build
#   idf.py -p COM12 flash monitor
#
# Success criteria after flash:
# - Boot log reports sensor mode 640x480 YUV422 6fps.
# - /api/camera/status reports effective_width=640, effective_height=480.
# - /api/camera/snapshot returns HTTP 200 with a valid JPEG.
# - Record capture_ms, jpeg_bytes, free PSRAM/internal heap, and face-detect
#   analysis latency when that pipeline is enabled.

# Override the stable OV2640 DVP choice from sdkconfig.defaults.
# CONFIG_CAMERA_OV2640_DVP_YUV422_240X240_25FPS is not set
CONFIG_CAMERA_OV2640_DVP_YUV422_640X480_6FPS=y
